# master-ci ai-integrity — scoped opt-outs, each with its reason.
# New production code outside these paths is held to the full blocking set
# (including the structural budgets under --enforce-bloat).
#
# 1. Fixtures/experiment class: the .op corpus under tests/, the lab
#    experiments, the playground web UI and the language-comparison apps
#    are fixtures-by-nature — master-ci's own repo excludes its fixtures/
#    the same way.
labs/
web/
tests/
apps/
packaging/
#
# 2. Recursive-descent cores: god-function / deep-nesting / long-file /
#    param-count ARE the architecture of a hand-written parser and its
#    differential oracle (SPEC documents the grammar the dispatch mirrors).
#    Guard-clause flattening would restructure 350k+ lines of verified
#    cores for zero behavior change. Everything else in the blocking set
#    (elided code, stubs, chatbot residue, debug residue, empty tests...)
#    stays ON for these paths.
check:god-function:src/
check:deep-nesting:src/
check:bloat-long-file:src/
check:bloat-param-count:src/
check:boilerplate-duplication:src/
# match-arm result construction (`Ok(Value::List(Rc::new(RefCell::new(out))))`
# and friends) is the interpreter-dispatch idiom: each arm builds its value
# inline; a shared constructor would add indirection across 40+ verified
# dispatch sites for zero behavior change.
check:god-function:bootstrap/
check:deep-nesting:bootstrap/
check:bloat-long-file:bootstrap/
check:bloat-param-count:bootstrap/
check:boilerplate-duplication:bootstrap/oracle.py
check:swallowed-exception:bootstrap/oracle.py
check:swallowed-exception:bootstrap/audit_builtins.py
check:god-function:scripts/
check:deep-nesting:scripts/
check:bloat-long-file:scripts/
check:bloat-param-count:scripts/
check:swallowed-exception:scripts/
